      "moduleId": "japanese-basics",
      "focus": "できます states ability; verbs can also have potential forms such as よみます → よめます (can read). ～てもいいですか asks permission; ～てはいけません prohibits an action. Here とって is the て-form of とります; learn the two とって phrases together for now, then study the て-form in lesson 20.",
